  40:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_fast_opt_q15.c **** /**
  41:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_fast_opt_q15.c ****  * @brief Convolution of Q15 sequences (fast version) for Cortex-M3 and Cortex-M4.
  42:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_fast_opt_q15.c ****  * @param[in] *pSrcA points to the first input sequence.
  43:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_fast_opt_q15.c ****  * @param[in] srcALen length of the first input sequence.
  44:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_fast_opt_q15.c ****  * @param[in] *pSrcB points to the second input sequence.
  45:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_fast_opt_q15.c ****  * @param[in] srcBLen length of the second input sequence.
  46:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_fast_opt_q15.c ****  * @param[out] *pDst points to the location where the output result is written.  Length srcALen+src
  47:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_fast_opt_q15.c ****  * @param[in]  *pScratch1 points to scratch buffer of size max(srcALen, srcBLen) + 2*min(srcALen, s
  48:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_fast_opt_q15.c ****  * @param[in]  *pScratch2 points to scratch buffer of size min(srcALen, srcBLen).
  49:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_fast_opt_q15.c ****  * @return none.
  50:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_fast_opt_q15.c ****  *
  51:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_fast_opt_q15.c ****  * \par Restrictions
  52:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_fast_opt_q15.c ****  *  If the silicon does not support unaligned memory access enable the macro UNALIGNED_SUPPORT_DISA
  53:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_fast_opt_q15.c ****  *	In this case input, output, scratch1 and scratch2 buffers should be aligned by 32-bit
  54:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_fast_opt_q15.c ****  *
  55:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_fast_opt_q15.c ****  * <b>Scaling and Overflow Behavior:</b>
  56:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_fast_opt_q15.c ****  *
  57:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_fast_opt_q15.c ****  * \par
  58:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_fast_opt_q15.c ****  * This fast version uses a 32-bit accumulator with 2.30 format.
  59:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_fast_opt_q15.c ****  * The accumulator maintains full precision of the intermediate multiplication results
  60:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_fast_opt_q15.c ****  * but provides only a single guard bit. There is no saturation on intermediate additions.
  61:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_fast_opt_q15.c ****  * Thus, if the accumulator overflows it wraps around and distorts the result.
  62:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_fast_opt_q15.c ****  * The input signals should be scaled down to avoid intermediate overflows.
  63:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_fast_opt_q15.c ****  * Scale down the inputs by log2(min(srcALen, srcBLen)) (log2 is read as log to the base 2) times t
  64:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_fast_opt_q15.c ****  * as maximum of min(srcALen, srcBLen) number of additions are carried internally.
  65:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_fast_opt_q15.c ****  * The 2.30 accumulator is right shifted by 15 bits and then saturated to 1.15 format to yield the 
  66:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_fast_opt_q15.c ****  *
  67:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_fast_opt_q15.c ****  * \par
  68:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_fast_opt_q15.c ****  * See <code>arm_conv_q15()</code> for a slower implementation of this function which uses 64-bit a
  69:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_fast_opt_q15.c ****  */
